## Context

The author agreed two tracks: a monthly public observatory and three academic contributions (JETP data paper, short historical comparison, long political economy with Christophe). The shared question is where JETPs stand and whether they accelerated project preparation and financing. Construction comparisons are premature.

Plan: `conception/jetp-observatory-and-papers-plan.md`. Programme tracker.

## First test

Integration acceptance exercise: follow one country total to project events and source locators, then reproduce a paper result from the exact frozen edition. A mismatched release, missing source or unsupported causal claim must fail review.

## Actions

Coordinate children 0726–0733 in the dependency order in the plan. Reuse 0715–0722 and 0711; do not duplicate collection or turn 0723 into a prerequisite. Record feasibility-led scope changes. This tracker remains open through an integration review.

The first programme milestone is now **M1**, accepted in two bounded steps:
[[0832]] published the four frozen country inventories without fusion; M1a itself is redefined by [[0834]] (2026-09-17): the MVP explores the data in three stages, documents, structured extraction and reconciled facts, with South Africa and Viet Nam as acceptance cases;
[[0833]] / M1b overlays stable canonical IDs, a common taxonomy and only
source-documented `same_as` / `component_of` relations. `possible_match` rows
remain separate and counted. Monthly refresh, source watching and match
resolution begin only after this base is accepted (the milestone that carries
them was renamed on 2026-09-29: see the next section).

## Milestones after M1 (redefined 2026-09-29)

Author decision, interactive. The instrument, then the measurement, then its
operation.

- **M2, the instrument.** An extraction pipeline that works on every document
  held (392 registered, 369 with a snapshot). Works means: it reproduces the
  lines of the 254 documents already extracted (replay, with every difference
  explained); re-running changes nothing and never renumbers a `line_id`; every
  document ends with lines or a recorded disposition; the code is polished by
  red-testing each extractor against a defect it must reject. Tracker
  [[1500]].
- **M3a, discover and freeze.** Discover all there is to discover at a cutoff
  date, under a stopping rule stated in advance, then freeze the registry.
  Two dates are published: the discovery cutoff (date of the last search) and
  the newest document date. Rounds are logged, empty ones included, and a
  known-item list gives a recall estimate. Draft rule: a fixed frame of
  channel classes per country and language; a secondary-to-primary pass that
  follows each quantitative claim of the main secondary trackers to its
  primary source (yielding a traceability rate); stop when two consecutive
  rounds in different channels add under 2 % new admitted documents and at
  least 90 % of the known-item list is recovered, with a pre-declared date and
  effort cap as backstop (numbers to be tuned). The list of unreachable
  sources is data, released with the registry. Acceptance: the author accepts
  the protocol, the recall estimate and the unreachable list before M3b starts.
- **M3b, extract, reconcile, release.** Extract the documents new since M2,
  reconcile with CRS and IATI ([[0721]]), join events, assets and outcomes
  ([[0723]]), release a dataset that cites its `release_id`. Reconciliation
  checks the ledger; it gives CRS and IATI no precedence over the source
  closest to the event (rule of [[1180]]).
- **M4, operation.** Scheduled refresh, link-rot, the pass launcher, shared code
  for AEDIST; the recurring machinery, whose deterministic part is checked by
  replay over the M3 release ([[1141]], [[1184]], weekly cadence of [[1140]]).
  Rule of two: shared code is extracted to `libs/` when a second consumer runs
  on it, not before.

## Exit criteria

- [x] M1a accepted: the MVP explores documents, extractions and facts end to end on the SA and VN acceptance cases ([[0834]]); the frozen inventories of [[0832]] are its input, not its result
- [ ] M1b bounded catalogue accepted without changing M1a or resolving `possible_match`
- [ ] M2 accepted: the extraction pipeline replays the 254 extracted documents and has run over all documents held ([[1500]])
- [ ] M3a accepted: registry frozen at a published cutoff, with protocol, recall estimate and unreachable list
- [ ] M3b released: dataset extracted, reconciled with CRS and IATI, joined, citing its `release_id`
- [ ] Children 0726–0733 delivered, or scope changes explicitly adjudicated
- [ ] Public observatory and repeatable monthly editions operational
- [ ] Citable dataset and three reviewable manuscripts linked to frozen releases
- [ ] Integration review checks source traceability, reproducibility and separation of observation from inference

## Validation

Apply the repository gates for the actual diff. Code work starts with the failing
fixture above; prose/data work records the documentary acceptance check. Preserve
source evidence and report limits rather than manufacturing a successful result.

